pandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Seasoning Ingredients</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoons</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Soy Sauce Powder</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for a savory flavor.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoons</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Miso Powder</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">adds depth and umami.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Garlic Powder</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">brings a fragrant kick.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Onion Powder</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">enhances the overall flavor.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Ginger Powder</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">offers a warm spice.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Salt</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">balances the seasoning.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Sugar</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">adds a hint of sweetness.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Dried Bonito Flakes</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for a rich, fishy taste.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Dried Seaweed Flakes</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">adds a touch of ocean flavor.</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-6198-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"6198\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Small bowl&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For mixing the seasoning.</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 whisk&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">To combine the ingredients.</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Airtight container&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For storing the seasoning.</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-6198-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-6198-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"6198\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Preparation Steps</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-6198-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Start by gathering all your ingredients. You’ll need garlic powder, onion powder, ginger powder, soy sauce powder, and a pinch of salt. Make sure everything is ready to go!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-6198-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">In a small bowl, add all the ingredients. Whisk them together until they are evenly mixed. You want a nice, uniform blend that smells amazing!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-6198-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Transfer your seasoning blend into an airtight container. This will keep it fresh and flavorful for your future ramen adventures!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-6198-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">When you’re ready to enjoy some ramen, add 1 to 2 tablespoons of your seasoning blend to 1 cup of hot broth. Stir well and serve immediately. Enjoy your delicious homemade ramen!</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-6198-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrient</th>\n<th>Amount per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>30</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>0g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>1g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>7g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sugar</td>\n<td>1g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Gather these simple ingredients to whip up your homemade <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ramen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ramen </a>seasoning!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Ramen-Seasoning-Ingredients-Display.webp\" alt=\"A collection of ramen seasoning ingredients displayed in small bowls on a wooden table, with a whisk nearby.\" class=\"wp-image-6196\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Ramen-Seasoning-Ingredients-Display.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Ramen-Seasoning-Ingredients-Display-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Soy Sauce Powder</strong> – 2 tablespoons – for a savory flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Miso Powder</strong> – 2 tablespoons – adds depth and umami.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Garlic Powder</strong> – 1 tablespoon – brings a fragrant kick.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Onion Powder</strong> – 1 tablespoon – enhances the overall flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Ginger Powder</strong> – 1 teaspoon – offers a warm spice.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Salt</strong> – 1 teaspoon – balances the seasoning.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Sugar</strong> – 1 teaspoon – adds a hint of sweetness.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Dried Bonito Flakes</strong> – 1 tablespoon – for a rich, fishy taste.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Dried Seaweed Flakes</strong> – 1 tablespoon – adds a touch of ocean flavor.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-ramen-seasoning\"><strong>How to Make Ramen Seasoning</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Making your own ramen seasoning is a fun and rewarding experience! With just a few simple ingredients, you can create a flavorful blend that elevates your ramen dishes. The preparation time is about 5 minutes, and there’s no cooking time involved. Just mix and store! This seasoning can be kept for a while, so you can enjoy it whenever you crave a warm bowl of ramen.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Homemade-Ramen-Seasoning-Ingredients-1.webp\" alt=\"Ingredients for ramen seasoning displayed in small bowls with a whisk on a wooden table.\" class=\"wp-image-6197\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Homemade-Ramen-Seasoning-Ingredients-1.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Homemade-Ramen-Seasoning-Ingredients-1-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Gather Your Ingredients</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Start by gathering all your ingredients. You’ll need garlic powder, onion powder, ginger powder, soy sauce powder, and a pinch of salt. Make sure everything is ready to go!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Whisk It Together</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a small bowl, add all the ingredients. Whisk them together until they are evenly mixed. You want a nice, uniform blend that smells amazing!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Store Your Seasoning</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Transfer your seasoning blend into an airtight container. This will keep it fresh and flavorful for your future ramen adventures!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Use Your Seasoning</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">When you’re ready to enjoy some ramen, add 1 to 2 tablespoons of your seasoning blend to 1 cup of hot broth. Stir well and serve immediately. Enjoy your delicious homemade ramen!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Condiment</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>Japanese</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>5 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>0 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>5 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Vegetarian</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>8</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>With hot broth for ramen</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-ramen-seasoning\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making Ramen Seasoning</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Experiment with different types of miso for unique flavors.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Adjust the saltiness by using low-sodium soy sauce.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add a pinch of sugar to balance the umami taste.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Incorporate dried seaweed for an authentic touch.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in an airtight container to keep it fresh longer.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-ramen-seasoning\"><strong>How to Serve this ramen seasoning</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Mix with hot broth for a quick soup base.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Sprinkle over stir-fried vegetables for extra flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use as a marinade for grilled chicken or tofu.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Blend into a dipping sauce for fresh spring rolls.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You can easily prepare and store your ramen seasoning for future use:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Ramen Seasoning Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Transfer leftovers to an airtight container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in the refrigerator for up to 2 weeks.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label the container with the date for easy tracking.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing Ramen Seasoning</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Portion the seasoning into freezer-safe bags or containers.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Remove excess air to prevent freezer burn.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date and use within 3 months for best quality.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating Ramen Seasoning</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw in the refrigerator overnight before reheating.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Heat gently in a saucepan over low heat, stirring frequently.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add a splash of water or broth if it seems too thick.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. What is in the ramen seasoning?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Ramen seasoning typically includes a blend of soy sauce, miso paste, garlic powder, onion powder, and sometimes sesame oil. You can also add chili flakes for a spicy kick or seaweed for an umami flavor. This combination creates a rich and savory base that enhances the overall taste of your ramen.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. What seasoning to use in ramen?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>For a delicious bowl of ramen, consider using soy sauce, miso, or a combination of both as your base seasoning. You can also incorporate garlic, ginger, and green onions for added flavor. If you want to experiment, try adding a dash of sesame oil or a sprinkle of furikake for an extra layer of taste.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. How to season ramen without a packet?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>You can easily season ramen without a packet by using pantry staples. Start with a base of soy sauce or miso, then add garlic powder, onion powder, and a bit of sesame oil. Adjust the flavors to your liking, and don’t forget to include fresh ingredients like green onions or bok choy for added freshness.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. What is 🍥 in ramen?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>The 🍥 symbol represents narutomaki, a type of Japanese fish cake often found in ramen. It’s characterized by its pink swirl and adds a unique texture and flavor to the dish. If you can’t find narutomaki, you can substitute it with other fish cakes or simply omit it for a delicious bowl of ramen.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Now that you’ve mastered homemade ramen seasoning, get ready to elevate your noodle game! It’s simple, rewarding, and oh-so-delicious. Each bowl will bring back cozy memories and warm your heart. So, gather your ingredients, unleash your creativity, and enjoy every slurp of your delightful ramen creation. Happy cooking!</p>\n",
